#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The owner's asks as the loop's miss signal (Evolve S1, docs/self-improvement-loop-2026-10-30.md).

    asks run [--days 7] [--digest FILE] [--no-model] [--no-overrules] [--dry-run]
    asks numbers [--days 7] [--json]
    asks baseline [--corpus DIR] [--model] [--refresh]
    asks ship <theme> <ref>
    asks merge [--dry-run] [--force]
    asks cusum [--days 60] [--json]
    asks golden add|list|check

Every improvement the owner asks for by hand is evidence the loop missed something. `run` is the
weekly pass (aurora's weekly-run runs it once a week, zero attended tokens):

  1 intake    `week-digest --json`: the owner's typed prompts, whole, every login dir, by their own
              time; a confidential scope's sessions are counted and never opened (its own pass reads them).
  2 sieve     a zero-token pre-label (machine / status / answer / ask / correction / task); a machine
              prompt (a launcher's, an IDE block, pasted content) is not the owner's and goes no further.
              A launcher's prompt is judged by the core's `transcript.machine_start`, the one rule
              week-digest applies before it (which already leaves those out and counts them); the
              sieve's own list is what the owner types that is no ask (`/autofinish`, `dispatch …`).
  3 classify  every other prompt through the gate: one batched call per dimension on the row
              `evolve.ask` — target (system | question | none), then kind, level and detectability for
              what is not `none`. `unknown` is a label. With the row off or the gate failing, the sieve's
              labels stand and the row says `by: sieve`.
  4 theme     asks are counted per (session, theme). One call on the row `evolve.theme` names each ask's
              theme as a kebab slug of the need (reusing the ledger's slugs), never the owner's words. Off
              or failing, a bag of hashed words matched by overlap stands in (F1 0.16 against the hand
              themes: the repeat share then reads low), so the ledger holds no prompt text: ids,
              counts, model slugs and short unsalted word hashes (a word list can reverse those: the state dir is the owner's).
  5 match     each detectable ask against the findings dated before it (the same need and a plausible
              intervention, never topic overlap), on the row `evolve.match`: `anticipated`, or the cause of
              the miss, M1–M7, or J (new information or a legitimate choice: kept, never in the
              denominator). No findings yet (S3/S5 write them): the step reports that and spends nothing.
              An earlier pass's detectable ask with no verdict yet (the matcher failed, or no findings
              then) is judged again while the digest still holds its prompt; one outside it stays unjudged.
  6 record    plumb's state dir (`asks/`): `asks.jsonl` one row per owner prompt (ids, labels, counts —
              never a prompt's text), `themes.json`, `overrules.jsonl` (the owner's memo and chat answers that went
              against the recommendation, from `interruptions`), `runs.jsonl` (what each pass cost).

`numbers` prints the rows `knowledge-numbers` shows: asks per 100 owner prompts, the detectable and J
shares, the repeat share over a 60-day lookback, recall and lead time once findings exist, and the
loop's cost. Recall is printed beside what it was judged over: each class's eligible (judged, not J),
the matcher's J (`judged_j`) and the not yet matched (`unmatched_eligible`), so a recall over few judged asks reads as such. `baseline` replays the 60-day model-labelled corpus (the owner's prompts, verbatim, on one
Mac only: read, never copied) through the sieve, and with --model through the gate, and prints the
agreement per dimension — counts only. `ship` records that a mechanism shipped for a theme.

Follow-ups (Evolve S11): `merge` is the theme ledger's merge pass, one `evolve.theme` call a month over the model
slugs (255 over 386 asks was the first baseline: the model names one need with different slugs across weeks, so
the repeat share read 15 % where the hand read 59 %); `run` makes it when it is due and the ledger holds enough
slugs, and `theme-merges.json` keeps old slug -> kept slug, which `numbers` follows. `numbers` reports G1's
three rows apart, eligible E and N asks (an N sensor adds nothing to E's recall), lead time as the finding's
time minus the ask's (negative when the loop was first). `cusum` replays the memo-acceptance CUSUM on the
owner's answers in timestamp order. `golden` is the fixture behind a change to the `evolve.ask` prompt or labels
(Ring 0): ids and verified labels in git (golden/manifest.json), the prompts' text only in the state dir.

The prompts, the labels and the matcher's causes are Ring 0 (docs/self-improvement-loop-2026-10-30.md):
they decide who counts as detectable, so only the owner changes them. Gate rows: the core's
settings/models.json (`evolve.ask`, `evolve.match`). State: ASKS_STATE, else <log dir>/plumb/asks.
"""
import argparse
import contextlib
import csv
import datetime as dt
